<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tonkin campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1886">1886</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tonkin campaign was the French military campaign of 1883 to 1886 to occupy Tonkin in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and establish a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> there. French forces fought Vietnamese troops, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-flag-army">Black Flag Army</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-yongfu">Liu Yongfu</a> and Chinese armies, and the campaign merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sino-french-war">Sino-French War</a> of 1884–1885. It ended with Tonkin under French control, later part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tonkin-campaign.jpg" alt="Tonkin campaign" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Images d'Epinal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prise_de_Bac-Ninh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
